  <text xml:lang="ta" type="edition">
    <body>

        <div xml:id="AN243.1-kilavi">
          <p type="edition">talaimakaṉ piriviṉkaṇ va<supplied>ṟ</supplied>puṟuttun tōḻikkut talaimakaḷ colliyatu.</p>
          <p type="translation" xml:lang="en">What SHE said [in order to say that she could bear it/not bear it] to the confidante who comforted [her] during the separation from HIM.</p>
        </div>
        <div rend="parallel">
      <lg xml:id="AN243.1">
        <l>avarai yāymala rutirat tuvariṉa</l>
        <l>vāṅkutuḷait tu<supplied>kili ṉīṅ</supplied>kai pūppa</l>
        <l>vīṅkupō taviḻnta vīrmputaṟ pakaṉṟaik</l>
        <l>kaṟaṅkunuṇ ṭuvalai yūruḻai yaṇiyap</l>
        <l>peyarnīr <supplied>pu</supplied>tuvār pīrciṉai nērpu</l>
        <l>viḷava<supplied>ri</supplied>n tiṟaiñciya piṟaṅkukatirk kaḻaṉi</l>
        <l>nelloli pācama ṟuḻaiik kalleṉak</l>
        <l>kaṭituvan tiṟutta kaṉṉi vāṭai</l>
        <l>neṭituvan taṉaiyeṉa <supplied>ni</supplied>l<supplied>lā</supplied> tēṅkip</l>
        <l>palapulan tuṟaiyun tuṇaiyil vāḻkkai</l>
        <l>namvalat taṉṉai kūṟi yavarnilai</l>
        <l>yaṟiyu<supplied>na</supplied> māyi ṉaṉṟumaṟ ṟilla</l>
        <l>paṉivār kaṇṇē māki yiṉiyatu</l>
        <l>namakkē yevva mā<supplied>ki</supplied>ṉ</l>
        <l>ṟaṉaittāṟ ṟōḻinan to<supplied>l</supplied>viṉaip payaṉē.</l>
      </lg>
      <lg type="translation" xml:lang="en">
        <l>While choice blossoms drop off the field bean, while the mimosa</l>
        <l corresp="1f">flowers like fine cloth, [its] curving orifices of coral [colour],</l>
        <l>while [with] the fizzling fine drops the Jalap in moist bushes</l>
        <l corresp="3f">that opened [their] swelling buds adorn the vicinity of the village,</l>
        <l corresp="8">“o virgin north wind that lingers after having come fast,</l>
        <l corresp="7">noisily stirring up the green growth of the paddy shoots</l>
        <l corresp="6">in the field with glistening ears that bow after the woodapple trees had been cut,</l>
        <l corresp="5">meeting the new branches of the sponge gourd overflowing with shifting water,</l>
        <l corresp="9">for a long time you have come”, thus lamenting without stopping</l>
        <l corresp="10">in a life without a mate when we stay, vexed in many [ways],</l>
        <l corresp="11">mother talking about our strength – his state,</l>
        <l corresp="12">if we were to know it, that would be good indeed.</l>
        <l corresp="13">Our eyes overflowing with tears, now it</l>
        <l corresp="14">has become trouble just to us.</l>
        <l corresp="15">Thus is, friend, the fruit of our old actions.</l>
      </lg>
        </div>
    </body>
  </text>

